==Strategy==
This stage has two waves of Dreadbores which will cause you to lose a lot of ground, along with an extremely threatening pusher in Medu-san.

The startoff can be stalled for money if you do not send out too many units. You can then build up a push and trigger the boss. Bring the Holy Blast cannon to unburrow the first Dreadbore and Gory. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] can provide solid defense, although the Medu-san and Dreadbore still can push.

[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] can subdue the bore, while spamming [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and/or [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] burst the Dreadbore down. [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] can help to push the Medu-San from attacking and save your attackers.

After the first Dreadbore dies, Medu-san will likely be in the middle of the stage. Use [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] on the second Dreadbore, and summon Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to temporarily kill Dreadbore and chunk at Medu-san. When Dreadbore revives, he will be at half health. Continue spamming your attackers and focus on meatshielding until Dreadbore dies, then take care of Medu-san for the win.

